A student writes the following C code to delete the **last node** of a DLL where `tail` points to the last node:

```c
void deleteLast(struct Node** head, struct Node** tail) {
    if (*tail == NULL) return;
    if (*tail == *head) { free(*tail); *head = *tail = NULL; return; }
    *tail = (*tail)->prev;
    free((*tail)->next);
    (*tail)->next = NULL;
}
```
Is this code correct?

**[HARD]** Analyze this C function that operates on a DLL where each node has `prev`, `data`, and `next`. What does `mystery()` do and what is the final list if input is `1 <-> 2 <-> 3 <-> 4 <-> NULL`?

```c
void mystery(struct Node* head) {
    struct Node* curr = head;
    while (curr != NULL) {
        struct Node* temp = curr->prev;
        curr->prev = curr->next;
        curr->next = temp;
        curr = curr->prev;
    }
}
```
